From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:51:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phylink: restore the error-pointer check in phylink_inband_caps

The internal PCS handling replaced the pristine IS_ERR_OR_NULL() check
with a plain non-NULL test, so an ERR_PTR() returned by .mac_select_pcs
is treated as a found PCS and dereferenced by phylink_pcs_inband_caps().

Restore the error check while keeping the upstream structure.

Adapted from ImmortalWrt-for-Gemtek-brightspeed commit 3fc77f2632.

Signed-off-by: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/phylink.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phylink.c
@@ -1020,7 +1020,7 @@
 	if (pl->mac_ops->mac_select_pcs) {
 		pcs = pl->mac_ops->mac_select_pcs(pl->config,
 						  interface);
-		pcs_found = !!pcs;
+		pcs_found = !IS_ERR_OR_NULL(pcs);
 	} else if (test_bit(interface, pl->config->pcs_interfaces)) {
 		list_for_each_entry(pcs, &pl->pcs_list, list) {
 			if (!phylink_validate_pcs_interface(pcs, interface)) {
